totoxics.\n...\nWith regards to conventional chemotherapy, studies in NSCLC, HBC, CRC and PDAC demonstrated that response rates to clinically used agents such as paclitaxel, carboplatin, gemcitabine, 5-fluorouracil, irinotecan and adriamycin, among others, are comparable between PDX models and clinical data (Table 3).\nMore recently, the role of PDX models as potential screening platforms for clinical trials has been also shown in a prospective study in PDAC.\nThis work showed that the combination of *nab*-paclitaxel and gemcitabine is effective in PDX models of PDAC, a finding that correlated with the clinical efficacy of this combination.\nIn fact, this regimen has recently been demonstrated to provide a survival benefit for patients with advanced PDAC in a randomized phase III study, and is likely to become a standard of care in this setting (38).", "date": "2014-07-15", "last_updated": "2026-08-21"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Page not found", "url": "https://medschool.cuanschutz.edu/colorado-cancer-center/clinical-trials/214C19E7-3028-64D9-A5BF-FF0A001CE385", "domain": "medschool.cuanschutz.edu", "snippet": "303-724-4357 (4-HELP from a campus phone)", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-18"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Patient-derived xenograft models: Current status ...", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2352304225000091", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "# Review ArticlePatient-derived xenograft models: Current status, challenges, and innovations in cancer research", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-10-07"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "OpenLB Open Library of Bioscience", "url": "https://ngdc.cncb.ac.cn/openlb/publication/OLB-PM-37602328", "domain": "ngdc.cncb.ac.cn", "snippet": "- Wafik S El-Deiry: Laboratory of Translational Oncology and Experimental Cancer Therapeutics, Warren Alpert Medical School, Brown University, Providence, RI, United States.", "date": "2023-01-01", "last_updated": "2025-07-01"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Evaluation of the safety, pharmacokinetics, and antitumor activity of ...", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S266636432500061X", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-09-06"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Patient-Derived Xenograft Models of Pancreatic Cancer - PMC", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7281668/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "In the gemcitabine refractory tumors, the combination treatment induced tumor regressions and suggested rigosertib could be a potential sensitizing agent in a subset of gemcitabine resistant tumors.\n...\nA reduction in tumor growth was observed in four of six models when treated with this single agent PLK4 inhibitor (*p* < 0.05).\n...\nThe data showed that gemcitabine or AZD7762 alone or in combination suppressed tumor growth in two subcutaneous pancreatic PDX models.", "date": "2020-05-22", "last_updated": "2026-08-27"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "A potential therapeutic target for pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0022356525397867", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-09-03"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "PLM-103 - Drug Targets, Indications, Patents - Patsnap Synapse", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/7b3e5bce8ca746e68b004c9c7068431f", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "Indication\nPhase\n...\nStudy\nPhase\nPopulation\nAnalyzed Enrollment\n...\nResults\nEvaluation\nPublication Date\nNo Data", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-05-11"}], "raw": {"id": "9d70b513-0dd1