{"row_id": "q047", "objective": "Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor first regulatory approval or market launch year for acute myeloid leukemia", "anchors": ["Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor", "CDK12"], "mode": "batch", "case_id": "q047-batch", "query": ["Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor Insilico Medicine AML approval launch", "Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor Insilico Medicine AML regulatory timeline", "Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor AML first market launch year"], "repeat": 0, "provider": "perplexity", "request": {"query": ["Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor Insilico Medicine AML approval launch", "Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor Insilico Medicine AML regulatory timeline", "Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor AML first market launch year"], "search_type": "web", "max_results": 10}, "ok": true, "status": 200, "error": null, "attempts": 1, "latency_ms": 872.8, "n_results": 10, "results": [{"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Press Releases", "url": "https://insilico.com/news", "domain": "insilico.com", "snippet": "20 October 2023\nInsilico Medicine nominates novel CDK12/13 small molecule inhibitor as preclinical candidate for multiple tumors", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-23"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "CDK12/13", "url": "https://insilico.com/pipeline_target_cdk12/13", "domain": "insilico.com", "snippet": "Cyclin-dependent kinase 12/13 (CDK12/13) Inhibitor:\nTreating Tumors through Induction of BRCAness\n(IND-Enabling)\nAssays Completed\nWholly-owned and Available for Licensing\n- *In vivo* efficacy studies – Combo study with Olaparib and Cisplatin\n- *In vivo* efficacy studies – Single agent\n- *In vivo* PK-PD\n- *In vivo* PK studies\n- *In vitro* ADMET studies\n- Developability/CMC\n- *In vitro* cell-based\n- Toxicology studies\n- Enzymatic\n...\nInsilico Medicine CDK12 Inhibitor Summary – IND-Enabling\n...\nEffective in both mono and combo therapies\n...\n- Potential broader indications such as AML, HCC, SCLC, Colorectal cancer, and Ovarian cancer\n...\n*In vivo* efficacy studies in SUM149PT CDX mice models showed strong dose-dependent anti-tumor activity with robust and durable tumor regression.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-22"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Insilico Medicine", "url": "https://siliconvalleyinvestclub.com/companies/insilico/tear-sheet.pdf", "domain": "siliconvalleyinvestclub.com", "snippet": "Insilico Medicine nominates novel CDK12/13 small molecule inhibitor as preclinical candidate for multiple tumors", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-30"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Pipeline | Insilico Medicine", "url": "https://insilico.com/pipeline", "domain": "insilico.com", "snippet": "Cyclin-dependent kinase 12 (CDK12) Inhibitor: Treating Tumors by Induction of BRCAness", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Insilico Medicine: Main", "url": "https://insilico.com/", "domain": "insilico.com", "snippet": "CDK12\nCyclin-dependent kinase 12 (CDK12) Inhibitor: Treating Tumors by Induction of BRCAness\nFGFR2/3\nFGFR2/3 Dual Inhibitor: Treatment of Solid Tumors", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Design, Synthesis, and Biological Evaluation of Novel Orally ...", "url": "https://colab.ws/articles/10.1021%2Facs.jmedchem.4c01616", "domain": "colab.ws", "snippet": "Publication date: 2025-02-14\n...\nHere, we report the discovery of compound 12b as a novel, potent, orally available covalent CDK12/13 dual inhibitor with a promising safety profile and robust in vivo antitumor properties.", "date": "2025-02-22", "last_updated": "2025-12-26"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "JMC｜With generative AI assistance, Insilico Medicine ...", "url": "https://www.eurekalert.org/news-releases/1074881", "domain": "eurekalert.org", "snippet": "Insilico Medicine (\"Insilico\"), a clinical stage generative artificial intelligence (AI)-driven biotechnology company, today announced the publication of a novel series of orally available covalent CDK12/13 dual inhibitors, as a potential option against refractory and treatment-resistant cancers.\nPublished in the ***Journal of Medicinal Chemistry* ** (IF=7.2), the study showcases the discovery of compound 12b, a potent, selective, and safe therapy targeting CDK12/13, empowered by Insilico’s proprietary generative AI platforms including PandaOmics and Chemistry42.\n...\nDuring the preclinical *in vitro* and *in vivo* testing, compound 12b demonstrated nanomolar potencies across cancer cell lines, desirable ADME properties.\nFurthermore, 12b exhibited significant efficacy in breast cancer and acute myeloid leukemia (AML) models, all without inducing intolerable side effects, paving the way for further therapeutic development.\n...\n\"The research and development process showcases how AI-guided drug design can achieve both precision and safety in cancer therapeutics, and we are striving to advance the compound in this program into clinical trials in the near future.\"", "date": "2025-02-26", "last_updated": "2026-04-21"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "CDK12 inhib News", "url": "https://sigma.larvol.com/moa.php?MoaId=777818&tab=newstrac", "domain": "sigma.larvol.com", "snippet": "Here, we report the discovery of compound 12b as a novel, potent, orally available covalent CDK12/13 dual inhibitor with a promising safety profile and robust in vivo antitumor properties.", "date": "2025-06-13", "last_updated": "2025-06-15"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Insilico Medicine News", "url": "https://sigma.larvol.com/company.php?CompanyId=968423&tab=newstrac", "domain": "sigma.larvol.com", "snippet": "Discovery and evaluation of ISM6466A, a novel covalent CDK12 inhibitor for the treatment of cancer\n...\nResults from a 28-day rat DRF study revealed that the compound did not show evident signs of toxicity at the tested doses, suggesting a reasonable safety window for ISM6466A.In summary, the novel, covalent, small-molecule CDK12 inhibitor, ISM6466A, demonstrated excellent preclinical efficacy along with favorable drug-like properties.\nOur results underscore the therapeutic potential of ISM6466A for the treatment of cancer.", "date": "2025-05-25", "last_updated": "2025-06-03"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "CDK12/13 TARGET therapy (InSilico Medicine) - Patsnap Synapse", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/d4f56c4afbbf4e43805fc7050386be8a", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "CDK12 inhibitors(cyclin dependent kinase 12 inhibitors),\n...\nDrug Highest Phase\nPreclinical\nFirst Approval Date\n...\nSolid tumor\nPreclinical\nChina\nInSilico Medicine Hong Kong Ltd.\n11 Jun 2024", "date": "2025-05-08", "last_updated": "2026-02-07"}], "raw": {"id": "b1e99faf-9a32-4f15-a483-1863abc5bf63"}, "ts": "2026-10-03T12:36:12+00:00"}
{"row_id": "q049", "objective": "ABSK131 in vivo single-agent monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression or shrinkage in MTAP-Deleted KRAS G12D-Mutated Pancreatic Ductal Adenocarcinoma animal models", "anchors": ["ABSK131"], "mode": "batch", "case_id": "q049-batch", "query": ["ABSK131 SU.86.86 monotherapy TGI", "ABSK131 PDAC xenograft monotherapy tumour regression", "ABSK131 KRAS G12D PDAC in vivo monotherapy", "ABSK131 MTAP-deleted pancreatic xenograft tumour volume"], "repeat": 0, "provider": "perplexity", "request": {"query": ["ABSK131 SU.86.86 monotherapy TGI", "ABSK131 PDAC xenograft monotherapy tumour regression", "ABSK131 KRAS G12D PDAC in vivo monotherapy", "ABSK131 MTAP-deleted pancreatic xenograft tumour volume"], "search_type": "web", "max_results": 10}, "ok": true, "status": 200, "error": null, "attempts": 1, "latency_ms": 1122.9, "n_results": 10, "results": [{"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "MTA-PRMT5 - Drugs, Indications, Patents", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/target/7a68e99130134dbc9048af6318b6a4c9", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "Results were shared for ABSK112 (EGFR exon20ins inhibitor), ABSK131 (PRMT5*MTA inhibitor), and ABK-KRAS-1 (pan-KRAS inhibitor), as well as results from a study investigating potential resistance mechanisms to KRAS G12C inhibitors.\n...\nThese strategies may restore sensitivity to KRAS G12C inhibitors and enhance clinical outcomes.\nTitle 3: The MTA-Cooperative PRMT5 Inhibitor ABSK131 Exhibits Potent Activity and Broad Synergistic Potential in MTAP-Deleted Cancer Models\n...\nABSK131 exhibits strong anti-tumor activity in MTAP-deleted lung and pancreatic cancer models and synergizes effectively with multiple therapeutic agents.\nThese findings support the continued clinical development of ABSK131 as both a monotherapy and in combination regimens for MTAP-deleted cancers.\n...\nTaken together, ABK-KRAS-1 exhibits broad in vitro activity against different KRAS mutations and induces dose-dependent tumor regression in KRAS mutated xenograft models.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-29"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "ABSK131 / Abbisko - LARVOL DELTA", "url": "https://delta.larvol.com/Products/?ProductId=77f15c4a-7852-4271-a722-b1143fb00c80", "domain": "delta.larvol.com", "snippet": "/ Abbisko\n...\n- \"In KRAS-mutant and MTAP-deleted models, ABSK131 led to robust tumor growth inhibition when combined with KRAS G12C inhibitor AMG510 or KRAS G12D inhibitor ABSK141.\n...\n(AACR 2026)\n...\n- \"ABSK131 exhibits strong anti-tumor activity in MTAP-deleted lung and pancreatic cancer models and synergizes effectively with multiple therapeutic agents.\nThese findings support the continued clinical development of ABSK131 as both a monotherapy and in combination regimens for MTAP-deleted cancers.\"\n...\nThese findings support the continued clinical development of ABSK131 as both a monotherapy and in combination regimens for MTAP-deleted cancers.\"", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-18"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Kras G12d", "url": "https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.2147/DDDT.S559325", "domain": "tandfonline.com", "snippet": "Preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials demonstrate meaningful antitumor activity, with emerging evidence of tumor microenvironment remodeling and delayed resistance.\n...\nThe *KRAS* G12D mutation is the most prevalent *KRAS* alteration in pancreatic cancer, making it a central focus of ongoing therapeutic development.\nZoldonrasib (RMC-9805), an oral covalent inhibitor designed to engage the active GTP-bound form of *KRAS* G12D, has also advanced into clinical testing (NCT06040541).\nPreliminary results presented at ASCO 2025 from the G12D–mutant PDAC cohort (40 evaluable patients) demonstrated encouraging antitumor activity, with an ORR of approximately 30% and disease control achieved in 80% of patients.^Citation36^ Pharmacodynamic analyses showed on-target activity, including reductions in *KRAS* G12D circulating tumor DNA (ctDNA) in responding patients.\n...\nEarly dose-escalation cohorts have demonstrated preliminary antitumor activity, and preclinical studies suggest synergistic effects when combined with proteasome inhibition with carfilzomib.^Citation37^ TSN1611 targets both GTP-bound (active) and GDP-bound (inactive) G12D and has demonstrated good tolerability with preliminary tumor shrinkage in refractory G12D–mutant tumors, including PDAC, non-small cell lung cancer, and colorectal cancer, in early phase I/II studies (NCT06385925).^Citation38^", "date": "2026-03-27", "last_updated": "2026-07-06"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "AACR 2026 | Abbisko Therapeutics Showcases Six Research Advances Highlighting pan-KRAS, 4th Generation EGFR, and Synthetic Lethality Approaches", "url": "https://www.biospace.com/press-releases/aacr-2026-abbisko-therapeutics-showcases-six-research-advances-highlighting-pan-kras-4th-generation-egfr-and-synthetic-lethality-approaches", "domain": "biospace.com", "snippet": "**MTA-cooperative PRMT5 inhibitor ABSK131**\nABSK131 is a potent and selective small-molecule MTA-cooperative PRMT5 inhibitor developed by Abbisko Therapeutics, targeting MTAP-deleted tumors, and is currently in clinical development.", "date": "2026-04-23", "last_updated": "2026-09-24"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Pan-cancer clinical and molecular landscape of MTAP ...", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2059702925004041", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-09-23"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "KRAS: the Achilles' heel of pancreas cancer biology", "url": "https://www.jci.org/articles/view/191939", "domain": "jci.org", "snippet": "The first KRAS^G12D^-selective inhibitor, MRTX1133, demonstrated near 1,000-fold selectivity for inhibiting KRAS^G12D^ signaling and *KRAS^G12D^*-mutant cancer cell growth as compared with KRAS WT (130, 131).\n...\nIn contrast to MRTX1133, zoldonrasib/RMC-9805 is a covalent ON KRAS^G12D^-selective inhibitor.\nZoldonrasib, a tri-complex inhibitor with CypA, binds to KRAS^G12D^ in its\nGTP-bound state and has demonstrated promising antitumor efficacy as both monotherapy and in combination with anti-PD1 therapy in preclinical KRAS^G12D^ models, including PDAC (133).\nEarly clinical evaluation showed promising efficacy in PDAC (30% ORR) with very limited toxicity (Table 3).", "date": "2025-08-15", "last_updated": "2026-10-03"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "AACR 2026 | Abbisko Therapeutics 展示了六項研究成果", "url": "https://news.futunn.com/hk/post/71909813/aacr-2026-abbisko-therapeutics-showcases-six-research-advances-highlighting-pan", "domain": "news.futunn.com", "snippet": "- Strong in vivo efficacy: Oral administration induced deep tumor regression in multiple KRAS G12V xenograft models, with robust target engagement.\n- 強大的體內療效：口服給藥在多種KRAS G12V異種移植模型中誘導了深度腫瘤消退，並展現了強勁的靶點結合能力。\n...\nABSK131是一種由Abbisko Therapeutics開發的強效且選擇性的小分子MTA協同PRMT5抑制劑，靶向MTAP缺失腫瘤，目前正處於臨床開發階段。", "date": "2026-04-23", "last_updated": "2026-04-23"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Abbisko Cayman Limited 和譽開曼有限責任公司", "url": "https://www.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2024/1023/2024102300933.pdf", "domain": "hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "These two research results demonstrated \nthe latest preclinical research progress of a potential best-in-class PRMT5*MTA inhibitor\nABSK131 and a potential best-in-class oral KRASG12D inhibitor ABSK141 from Abbisko \nTherapeutics pipeline.\n...\nUtilizing structural and computation-aided medicinal chemistry design, we have discovered a potential best-in-class\nMTA-cooperative PRMT5 inhibitor ABSK131 with improved potency, selectivity, and brain-penetrant ability.\n...\nABSK131, presented here by Abbisko Therapeutics, is a highly selective MTA-cooperative and brain-penetrant PRMT5 inhibitor.\nIts superior profile supports its advancement into clinical studies.\n...\nABSK141 demonstrated high binding affinity and good biochemical activity to KRASG12D in vitro.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-10-08"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "�Z6���K�X}е���{�_O=���\"�f<����]o��:�)[wWAG�0J��^��a��MRF�i�9?`�q��N^�������K���Ȝ�k�1f��''�j�)�cS��{�-�ܜ��ȷ:�� w��U�@Մ�q� z2Ҽ���%�{:��Qc�{'A?k�} *�#c�}.fk�*���)9_��8;8��;�vw��5��jPRJWI�rH� ���`n�_�D�y�ڷ.�5�K�>'J~��w��IǍY��Y����F� ���b���lZ}FY�zp��_8����1���71���c�*m�.UI� 4�j�,�H�# ���w�XXM�L\\�D8��������a̻��j�?�JIxBP8��<�U�j jrE�G/ˬ8Ț��2�C&c�ZwD�ƅ��ך}h��\"��z����?4�m�N:���LNFf��Y�,�~�Y�mK��o�X�O-�Ճ��9��LQt)g댛��W��2�5��(�e�J��52H�4s?NJϥ�y`�g���\\_���2�r5 \\m���l�$rw�1����!�iq�A����v��K�y3N�ߵ�V�S�����L��3 ���ͽ�852���I���`�S�����b��,~����G�����A�P)�ϰ6�ͱ�N��;�3�t����@�����^4��-��9&�P0�]ELu��A��1�^���J�J��Rm9���L�ك��cx *F�\"� �VC~�B%��ЁPW0c��8�9Ԡ�w�jHO>�����S��k�� �p:��g�R�>���5h�Eoo�ysU���� G�,�(����~?�ڻ�5�<���T����k�9�G���!~����s^+ʓ{ �tyr6��:��l�`~+�S��!D��Qv��d0���um� bN�� df@c�������H6���w�[q!�����HO�s�z�t����l��o���(6��Hr���d�� ��S�A���@��o18�2��l�<�B�T�A�pF�J�����JP� �0�mr��M*-f�������+��P2����<-�h�Y��ҿ�Qr~/&J���g&��0ch4&'%f4�й��.$�Hͮn���-����zo��g��!�Fy���w^��[0�����hå ƒ蚏�$���bl��wر$�za�w�G��%DM���(k�iެ��jfVY�۬�Y1%��?���aO�fa�z�S�`�t��h�v9t�k��Қ_�����sD��XŸ��ӕ�I12�T�2;�J��� B#P̠,B�Q>���6�c\\nu��沸Ž@m.���S�4|��O�|�n�*F7څ�S�f��&���a�Y��c�y�yCLs93������Y��;W� �B�WU'�����D�������c��c�S ӭq�n f0{��Iv����Z�`� ?;(Ȝ�i�¹��Ѱ:�(Ҭ��� �#�C 8��R4 B��5ˣV������uʯd��b9@���J������&v)J��!�ުS|������?���A�on������d�:t_E�<�/|���~����U���p���vr��~�s£K{���;��Q�z�rr�����$�,&�����$�������h������Kw������Ȭl7�^َ�x.'s�:�:�S&��M�-K-�;Yɑ}�q͉-��Ƥ���#H�6O��o8+�{�������$ߕ����dAо��B�ٿʺzmޙ�d~VU��%�u� �K�/���!Z��R-�ڧä�>���j�s���pI�ث��%^J��+o��[Y�žh$���m7Ase�R���U���_����g��,�[ׯ�ո��p ���xr���볛�������I���W�a�-���$9 5'rtƶ�b�w����A�H�J�*�����3���-M�;�lP'm�F*��hE����lKI��:3��� �k�v���